{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion-Factor Chains.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion-Factor Chains.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conversion factor chains conversion factor chains","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion-Factor Chains.md","fileName":"Conversion-Factor Chains.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conversion-Factor Chains","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Unit Algebra and Measurement Precision]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Unit Algebra and Measurement Precision","Unit Conversion Factor","Dimensional Homogeneity in Equations","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion-Factor Chains.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion-Factor Chains.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conversion factor chains conversion factor chains","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion-Factor Chains.md","fileName":"Conversion-Factor Chains.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conversion-Factor Chains","heading":"Conversion-Factor Chains","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"When no convenient direct factor is used, several compatible ratios can be multiplied in sequence. The book converts nautical miles to fathoms through kilometers and meters: $\\mathrm{nmi}\\times\\mathrm{km/nmi}\\times\\mathrm{m/km}\\times\\mathrm{ftm/m}$ leaves only fathoms. The intermediate units cancel regardless of the values carried by their factors. Writing the units alongside each ratio exposes a reversed factor or missing step before a calculator result is accepted. See [[Unit Conversion Factor]] and [[Dimensional Homogeneity in Equations]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Unit Algebra and Measurement Precision","Unit Conversion Factor","Dimensional Homogene